35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's clear the room is currently useless for privacy. The walls are paper-thin, and people are eating at their desks anyway.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We've spent 68,000 yen on outside rentals for tiny groups. It seems we really need a dedicated space for meetings.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It's not fair! Only the people sitting by the door use it, and the fridge is always a disaster!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are strangers in our own office. Our difficult conversations happen in public, leaving scars that last for weeks.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We waste nearly an hour a day on lunch trips, and the equipment in these rooms is a constant drain on facilities.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, if we spend 141,000 on a meeting room, does that stop the monthly bleed of rental fees?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"It should. The rental costs are adding up, and the meeting fit-out is more expensive but might be a better investment.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But if we make it a kitchen, we can stop the crumbs on the keyboards! I saw them!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"A kitchen is for nourishment, but a meeting space can be for healing and honest dialogue.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,A kitchen requires the most upkeep. We already have a history of people ignoring the fridge.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"A quiet room would solve the noise, but it doesn't solve the ""eating at desks"" problem or the rental costs.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried about who signs for the cost... but the rental fees are already happening. A meeting space seems most urgent.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want to be the only one cleaning up again! If it's a meeting room, is it cleaner?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,A bookable space ensures accountability. It gives us a sanctuary for the things that cannot be said at a desk.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The time lost to lunch is significant. However, the maintenance of a kitchen is a hidden cost in hours.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Logically, the meeting space solves the rental cost and the privacy issue, provided we fix the wall.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think I agree. It seems the most practical for the budget in the long run.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I still think a kitchen is fun, but I hate cleaning. Maybe a meeting room is better?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us choose the path that brings us together with dignity and privacy.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will support the option that minimizes unplanned maintenance and wasted movement.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
